        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johannes Vermeer\n- Works: The Lacemaker, The Music Lesson\n- Places: Louvre, Paris\n- Concepts: Dutch painting, domestic interior scenes, bobbin lace\n\nFacts:\n- Johannes Vermeer was a Dutch painter born in October 1632 and died in December 1675.\n- Johannes Vermeer specialized in domestic interior scenes of middle-class life.\n- The Lacemaker is a painting by Johannes Vermeer completed around 1669–1670.\n- The Lacemaker is held in the Louvre in Paris.\n- The Lacemaker shows a young woman in a yellow shawl holding bobbins and placing a pin in a pillow while making bobbin lace.\n- The Music Lesson, also called Lady at the Virginals with a Gentleman, is a painting by Johannes Vermeer.\n- The Music Lesson depicts a young female pupil receiving a music lesson.",
